course: dictionary
lesson: 9301
title: Speciality: the thing you are famous for
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A speciality is something a person or place is especially good at or known for. A café's speciality is its best dish, and a doctor's speciality is their special area of medicine.
explain: Look at the context to find the meaning that fits. «Each wild cat has its own speciality: the leopard is the strong climber that drags its meal up a tree, the jaguar has the crushing bite that cracks turtle shells, and the cheetah is the sprinter, the fastest runner on land.» The clues are climber, bite and runner, so a speciality is the thing each cat is best at.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it in. Try "Each wild cat is best at its own special thing." If that still makes sense, you have found the right meaning.
fact: Speciality means a thing someone or somewhere is especially good at or known for.
fact: «Cornish pasties» are a speciality of Cornwall, so they are the food Cornwall is famous for.
fact: In a café, the speciality is the dish it makes very well and is known for.
fact: A doctor's speciality is their special area of medicine, such as heart medicine.
fact: Speciality is a noun, and its plural is specialities.
exercise: «Each wild cat has its own speciality.» What does speciality mean here? | A loud noise a cat makes | A kind of tree in the jungle | *The thing each cat is especially good at | A pet that lives in the house
exercise: «A café's speciality is its best dish.» What does speciality mean in this sentence? | A table by the window | *The dish the café is famous for and makes very well | A friendly waiter | The cheapest drink on the menu
exercise: Find and copy one word from the cat sentence that means a very fast runner. | climber | bite | *sprinter | turtle
test: «Cornish pasties are a speciality of Cornwall.» What does this tell you? | Cornwall has no food at all | *Cornwall is famous for making pasties very well | Pasties are always eaten cold in the sea | Pasties are a kind of bird found in Cornwall
test: «Dr Patel's speciality is heart medicine.» What is her speciality? | The name of her car | A tiny hospital room | *Her special area of medicine, which is the heart | Her favourite colour
exam: Which sentence uses speciality to mean a dish a place is famous for? | "The leopard drags its meal up a tree." | "The jaguar has a crushing bite." | *"The café's speciality is its lemon cake." | "The cheetah is the fastest runner on land."
